<title>MEXICO: Banco International places 3-year bond.</title>
<headline>Banco International places 3-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco International S.A., a subsidiary of Grupo Financiero Bital S.A., said on Friday that it had placed a $100 million three-year floating bond at a rate of LIBOR plus 275 basis points.</p>
<p>In a statement, the bank said the bond is backed by the flow of funds that it receives from its clients.</p>
<p>The bond was placed on August 29.</p>
<p>The bank said bond rating agency Duff &amp; Phelps gave the bond an investment-grade rating of BBB.</p>
<p>The issue was lead by SBC Warburg Inc, a subsidiary of Swiss Bank Corp.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City Newroom (525) 728 9559</p>
</text>
